+# Audit: the model's answer (0.23.1)
+
+Date: 2026-11-03 · PR: Cochilo 0.30.0 · Auditor: Claude (graphic-design-fundamentals + impeccable)
+
+## Scope
+
+A variant of the Conversation answer card for text written by an on-device model, and a
+"thinking" card. Existing roles only; no tokens.
+
+## graphic-design-fundamentals (§13 checklist)
+
+| # | Question | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Brief | Pass: a generated answer can never pass for a reviewed one |
+| 2 | Concept | Pass: same card, plus a label that says who wrote it |
+| 3 | Hierarchy | Pass: the answer first, the label after, in meta |
+| 4 | Contrast | Pass: listed pairs |
+| 5 | Alignment and grid | Pass |
+| 6 | Spacing | Pass: space3 between answer and label |
+| 7 | Typography | Pass |
+| 8 | Colour | Pass: no new colour; no "AI" sparkle |
+| 9 | Consistency | Pass |
+| 10 | Simplicity | Pass |
+| 11 | Real-size test | Pass: Cochilo `ask_generated_light` |
+| 12 | Accessibility and ergonomics | Pass: live regions for thinking and the answer |
+| 13 | Production | Pass |
+
+## impeccable (audit)
+
+| # | Dimension | Score | Key finding |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Accessibility | 4 | Label read with the answer |
+| 2 | Performance | 4 | — |
+| 3 | Appearance & theming | 4 | Roles only |
+| 4 | Platform conformance | 4 | — |
+| 5 | Adaptivity | 4 | — |
+| | **Total** | **20/20** | |
